  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of Multi-Purpose Cash Assistance to Vulnerable IDP Households in Yemen (Rapid Response Mechanism), Priority 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2021, 491,000 people were displaced in Yemen due to protracted and intensified conflict (HNO 2022), and in the first five months of 2022, over 42,000 people have been displaced. Additionally, the conflict in Ukraine has impacted the rise of food prices, compounding the pre-existing food insecurity for vulnerable groups across Yemen. The deteriorating economic conditions in Yemen have placed an additional burden on vulnerable groups, including women, children and persons with disabilities, to adopt negative coping strategies, including incurring significant debt burdens, agreeing to early marriage and, with constrained access to basic services, becoming even more dependent on external assistance. In this project, IOM aims to improve the living conditions of newly displaced crisis affected households and families affected by disasters related to natural hazards through the provision of multi-purpose cash assistance as part of the rapid response mechanism assistance package.</narrative>
  </description>
